Subject: Cantor EVO-X2 Scratch Build Executor P0 Deployment Controller Design

@ [design_uuid] 5003ce44-4246-49e5-9cdd-4675a6918470
@ [canonical_uuid] 935e020f-8c6f-49e4-b355-63eabd3b778b
@ [package_evidence_commit] 4dc154234cd88c192495126a4374d74616ca0c3f
@ [package_evidence_bookend_commit] 9e583948ea6c1f52604862c354e99d8ccb1195ba

& [Problem]
  + the corrected package and host harness are published, but a bounded local controller does not yet compile exact deployment, retrieval, refusal, verification, and transient-cleanup ordering
  + the host harness deliberately cannot issue a conservation receipt when provider observation itself is unavailable; that boundary must remain visible instead of fabricating hashes

& [Decision]
  + compile a pure typed ten-stage plan before implementing any SSH, SCP, filesystem, process, or network effect wrapper
  + bind run UUID, corrected package implementation evidence and immediate-bookend commits, package-set SHA256, future controller implementation and immediate-bookend commits, local evidence root, transport archive, staging root, service, workspace, target, and fixed host alias
  + distinguish operational_refusal_before_commission_no_receipt from an admitted host-harness failed or refused receipt
  + require every stage to stop on failure and allow transient transport cleanup only after independent local evidence verification

& [TenStages]
  + local_package_verify
  + publication_lineage_verify
  + remote_preflight
  + transfer_package
  + remote_package_verify
  + atomic_service_install
  + execute_commission_once
  + retrieve_evidence
  + independent_local_verify
  + cleanup_transient_transport

& [Authority]
  + plans are descriptive_not_authorizing, remote_contact_authorized false, and effects 0
  + effectful-stage labels name authority that a later separately published wrapper and commission must prove; they do not grant it

& [Delineation]
  + included: strict pure request plan verification forms, deterministic CLI, checked fixture, independent evidence, adversarial tests
  + excluded: SSH or SCP launch, remote observation, archive transfer, service install, host harness execution, receipt retrieval, transport deletion, provider mutation, retry, and autonomous work
